/* ============================================================
   DukanList Service Worker
   Strategy:
     - install : precache key static assets
     - fetch   : network-first, fallback to cache
     - skip    : /admin/*, /panel/*, supabase API, POSTs, non-GET
   ============================================================ */
const VERSION    = 'dukan-v3.25.0';  // GOLDEN PAGES MANAGE PAGE — user asked 'mere paas admin me ye list kaha par aayegi and edit delete type option kaise rahenge?' db/170 adds 4 admin-only RPCs: admin_gp_list_all (paginated + filterable by city/category/search/no-mobile/no-owner + returns help_request_count + total_count for pagination), admin_gp_update_soft (whitelisted edit — name/name_hi/owner_name/mobile/area/city/categories[]/primary/notes — with multi-category junction swap; only operates on status='soft_listed' so it can't accidentally fall over onto live listings), admin_gp_delete_soft (hard delete, safe because soft listings are reference entries with no customer data — refuses if status was promoted), admin_gp_promote_to_full (graduate to main DukanList — accepts target='pending' for admin moderation queue or 'active' for direct publish). All 4 gate on is_admin(). New /admin/golden-pages-manage.html: filter bar with search input + city dropdown + category dropdown + chip filters (All / No mobile / No owner / Has help requests); paginated 25/page list with prev/next; per-row card showing name + Hindi + category + city + area + added-time + owner + mobile + status badges (Mobile/Owner/Hindi/Help requests count) + 4 action buttons (Edit blue, Promote green, Claim link amber, Delete red); full edit modal with all fields + multi-cat picker (search → click chip to add, click selected to promote to primary, × to remove) + city chip selector + save/cancel with error handling. Toast feedback (green success / red error / dark info). Top nav links between Add and Manage pages — both pages now have shared 3-link nav. Confirm-required promote (with type 'pending' or 'active' choice) and delete actions. Empty states for no-results and load-failure. Mobile responsive — actions stack into single column below 560px. Admin can now sit on one screen and review/edit/promote 100s of soft listings.  // Golden Pages — Owner Name optional input (db/169 + form field). User asked 'owner ka naam optional de do na form me' — db/168 had only made the column nullable but the RPC didn't accept the field as a parameter at all. db/169 drops + recreates admin_soft_add_shop with p_owner_name TEXT DEFAULT NULL appended (now 10 params). Trim + treat empty string as NULL via NULLIF(TRIM(COALESCE(p_owner_name,'')), ''). Insert sets businesses.owner_name to clean trimmed value or NULL. /admin/golden-pages-add.html: new 👤 Owner Name field inserted between Area and Mobile (optional) — hint reads 'If you know the owner\\'s name from reference, add it here. Helps personalisation when they claim.' submitSingle now reads f_owner_name + passes p_owner_name to RPC. Save&Next and resetSingleForm both clear the field on next iteration. Bulk paste mode still skips owner name (multiple shops per batch, owner varies — doesn't make sense to share one).  // HOTFIX — businesses.owner_name was declared NOT NULL in db/01 but soft-listed / pre-listed flows legitimately don't have an owner name at insert time (those are reference-based directory entries; the actual owner is discovered via claim flow later). User hit '400 — null value in column owner_name violates not-null constraint' when adding 'Premi Desi Ghee Bhandhar' via Golden Pages. db/168 issues ALTER TABLE businesses ALTER COLUMN owner_name DROP NOT NULL — non-destructive, no data lost, existing rows still have their values, but new INSERTs from admin_soft_add_shop / admin_pre_list_shop / admin_soft_bulk_add can now leave it NULL. All downstream readers (business.html, card.html, admin/shop.html, digital-card.html) already handle null/empty owner_name with sensible fallbacks (display the shop name if owner_name absent), so no UI changes needed. register_business_public continues to require owner_name from the form — public registration UX unchanged. Column comment updated to document the new semantics.  // HOTFIX — City chips empty on /admin/golden-pages-add.html. User screenshot showed only the 'CITY *' label with no chips below. Root cause: loadCities() queried .select('id, name, slug') on geo_cities, but geo_cities table (per db/01) has NO slug column — only id, name, name_hi. Supabase silently failed the query (caught by try/catch), CITY_LIST stayed empty, renderCityChips skipped all DEFAULT_CITIES since no match was found. Three fixes in admin/golden-pages-add.html: (1) loadCities now selects only existing columns (id, name, name_hi) + logs the actual error to console instead of silently swallowing — admin can debug if it still fails. (2) renderCityChips matching now uses ONLY case-insensitive name comparison (slug-based check removed since column doesn't exist). (3) After rendering the preferred DEFAULT_CITIES, the function now ALSO appends any OTHER cities returned by the DB query — so if admin has seeded custom cities (or my DEFAULT_CITIES list is missing one), they still appear as chips instead of being silently hidden. (4) If matching falls through entirely (DB returned empty / errored), the chip area shows a red warning banner pointing to the console instead of a blank space — no more 'CITY *' label hanging alone with nothing below it.  // GOLDEN PAGES form upgrade (db/167 + admin/golden-pages-add.html overhaul). User feedback on the soft-add form: (1) city selector missing → silently defaulted to Mandi Dabwali; (2) only one category could be added; (3) 'Shop Name' label too narrow — Golden Pages also covers schools, clinics, organisations, sansthayen. db/167 drops + recreates admin_soft_add_shop with multi-cat signature: p_category_slugs TEXT[], p_primary_category_slug, p_name_hi (optional Hindi name), p_city_id, plus existing fields. Validation: 1-5 cats, dedup + lowercase, primary defaults to array[0] if not in selection. Inserts into business_categories junction with is_primary flag; businesses.category_id/sub_category_id mirror primary for backward compat. Also adds admin_gp_recent_soft_listings(p_limit) — returns last N soft listings added in past 2 hours for the recent-activity panel. admin/golden-pages-add.html rewritten: field label 'Shop Name' → 'Name' with inclusive hint 'Shop, clinic, school, organisation — anything in town'; new optional 'Name in Hindi' field; new city chip selector (Mandi Dabwali default + Sirsa/Bathinda/Mansa/Muktsar — same DEFAULT_CITIES pattern as quick-add-shop); new multi-cat picker — replaces single-cat select with chip list of up to 5 selected categories, first one is ⭐ primary, click any non-primary to promote, × button to remove individually; new 'Save & Add Another' button beside primary submit — clears name fields but keeps category+city+source so admin can chain-add 20 shops in 2 minutes; new amber 'Recently added (last 2 hours)' panel at top of form showing what's been added across the team for situational awareness; mobile placeholder updated to '10-digit Indian number' (English-only); hint translated 'Optional. Agar pata ho...' → 'If you have it, add now — owners can claim faster later'; source placeholder expanded with examples; bulk-add tab also gets city chip selector + same updates. Net effect: ground operation now scales — admin can sit with a Vyapar Mandal list and bulk-add 100+ shops per hour properly categorized + correctly geolocated to the right city.  // GOLDEN PAGES polish + homepage promotion. (1) golden-pages.html copy fully translated to clean English: hero sub now reads 'Every shop in Mandi Dabwali, Sirsa & Bathinda — aadti, doctors, schools, organisations & more, all in one place', search placeholder 'Search any shop, area or category', meta defaults from '—' to '0' so blank state reads cleanly even before stats RPC resolves, footer CTA title 'Want to list your shop?' / body 'Build your full DukanList profile — photos, hours, reviews, contact form, everything customers need. Free forever.', empty grouped state now includes an inline 'Open DukanList' button so users have a clear next step, empty flat-list message 'Try a different category or search term.', notify modal title 'Help us reach this shop' + sub 'Your request goes to the DukanList team. We\\'ll personally contact the owner and ask them to claim this listing.' + textarea placeholder 'I\\'m a customer and need their contact details...', shop card buttons now 'I\\'m the owner' (claim) and 'Request contact' (notify) — clearer than the previous Hinglish 'Owner? Claim' / 'Help us reach'. (2) Loading text 'Loading the directory…' (en-dash). (3) MAIN PAGE INTEGRATION — added a new golden-pages-pill on index.html right after the pucho-bhai-mega-pill in .hero-extras row. Saffron gold gradient (#78350F → #92400E → #D97706) matching DukanList brand palette + Golden Pages identity. 🥇 icon + 'Golden Pages' bold + '→ Town Directory' CTA chip. Bilingual via data-i18n-en/hi (English-led with Hindi 'गोल्डन पेजेस'). Subtle shine animation (3s gradient pan), hover lift + scale 1.03, 2px gold border ring. Inline scoped CSS so no main.css changes. Mobile responsive — pads/font shrink at 480px. Sits one-line with Pucho Bhai pill saving vertical space as requested.  // GOLDEN PAGES SOFT-LISTING DIRECTORY (db/166 + admin + public). Reference-based bulk directory that lives separately from main DukanList — admin adds 100s of shops with just name + category + area (mobile optional), and these appear ONLY on /golden-pages.html until owner claims and upgrades. ARCHITECTURE: introduced new businesses.status value 'soft_listed' (extended CHECK constraint to allow it). Critical design choice — almost every public RPC + JS query already filters by status='active', so soft listings are AUTOMATICALLY invisible from main DukanList everywhere with ZERO changes needed across ~10 existing query sites. When owner claims via existing claim flow, status flips 'soft_listed' → 'pending' (joins normal moderation queue + email gate). New gp_help_reach_log table for customer-driven nudge requests. 7 new RPCs: admin_soft_add_shop (single, mobile optional), admin_soft_bulk_add (paste up to 500 names with shared category+area, per-name try/catch with skip reasons), gp_list_shops (public paginated with category/city/search filters), gp_categories_with_counts (browse), gp_stats, gp_help_reach (anon, light fingerprint dedup), admin_gp_help_requests (admin queue of customer nudges). New /admin/golden-pages-add.html — gold/saffron themed admin tool with stats strip + 2 tabs: Single (name + category search chips + optional area/mobile/source) and Bulk Paste (one shared category + area + textarea for 100s of names with live count). New /golden-pages.html — public directory with gold hero, search box, category chips, grouped-by-category default view (top 8 cats × 6 shops each with View all link), flat-list view when category/search active, per-shop card with 👋 Owner Claim button (links to existing claim.html?token=...) and 📞 Help Us Reach button (opens modal → gp_help_reach RPC with optional customer note + browser fingerprint hash for dedup). Footer CTA links to register.html for full registration upsell. URL #shop=slug supports deep-linking. Full bilingual (English-led with Hinglish hints). Mobile-responsive. Ready for ground operation: aap reference se 1000 shops 1 hafte me add kar sakte ho.  // HOTFIX — user reported 'window.DukanAlgo.getDailyTheme is not a function' crash on Discover open after v3.5.0 deploy. Root cause: discover-algo.js was referenced without a version query string so service worker served the cached pre-Phase-2 file (which doesn't have getDailyTheme) while discover.html was the new version calling it. Two fixes: (1) discover.html script tag now references /assets/js/discover-algo.js?v=v3.5.0 — the query string forces SW to fetch fresh. Bump this every time the algo file gains new public methods. (2) Defensive fallbacks in discover.html init around all new Phase 2 calls: typeof window.DukanAlgo.getDailyTheme === 'function' guard before getDailyTheme(), countMatching(), matchesTheme(). If older algo is somehow still loaded, theme stays null, themeCount stays 0, theme pill hides, and feed falls back to plain rankShops or random shuffle — no crash. console.warn for visibility. Code change in /assets/js/discover-algo.js itself was correct — only consumption needed hardening.  // DISCOVER PHASE 2 — Daily Theme bundles (Spotify Daily Mix style). discover-algo.js gets new DukanAlgo.getDailyTheme() returning a theme object based on weekday: Sunday=🏆 Top of Town (engagement-weighted), Monday=🆕 Fresh Faces (created/pre_listed <7d), Tuesday=⭐ Top Rated (4.5★+ with 5+ reviews), Wednesday=🎁 Today\'s Deals (featured_until proxy), Thursday=🍱 Food & Cravings (slug/name pattern match), Friday=💍 Weekend Prep (wedding vendor patterns), Saturday=🛍 Shop Local (retail patterns). Each theme has emoji, title, sub, gradient (CSS), accent, and a match() function returning 0..1. Helper THEME_PATTERNS map covers food/wedding/shop_local/health with 20+ slug substrings + a regex on category names so coverage scales as categories grow. New helpers: themeBoost(shop, theme), countMatching(shops, theme), matchesTheme(shop, theme). rankShops now takes opts.theme — matching shops get up to +12 pts boost; perfect matches (>=0.9) get a 'XX Theme pick' reason prepended for the Why sheet. discover.html integration: STATE gets new theme/themeCount/themeFilter fields, populated in init from the algo. buildChips inserts a new chip-theme pill FIRST (only when themeCount >= 3 — avoids dead-end filter) with the theme gradient, count badge, and a pulsing box-shadow animation; chip click handler now routes data-theme-pill to STATE.themeFilter toggle (clears category filter, theme wins). renderFiltered runs theme filter pass first. Empty-state CTA + reset button now clear themeFilter too. NEW one-time-per-day celebration toast (.theme-celebration) — pill-shaped pop appearing at the top after feed loads, gradient bg matching theme, shows '‘Today’s vibe — Food & Cravings · 12 shops' with auto-dismiss after 4s; tappable to apply filter; close × button. Seen state stored under dl_theme_seen_<id> = YYYY-MM-DD so it only appears once per day per theme. Result: feed automatically surfaces relevant shops per day without manual curation — Thursday lunch you naturally see dhabas higher, Friday you see decorators, Sunday you see top performers.  // Why sheet + algo reasons fully English-ified. User asked for English UI on the Discover Why sheet. Updated all copy: sheet title ('Why are you seeing this shop?'), subtitle ('stored only on your phone, never sent to our servers'), action buttons ('Show more like this' / 'Hide this shop'), reset confirm/toast strings, and all reason strings in discover-algo.js — 'Only X km from you', 'You\'ve been viewing this type of shop', 'Joined X days ago' (with day/days grammar), 'X people viewed this', 'It\'s food time right now', 'Service hours right now', new 'Clinic hours right now' for healthcare bucket. Fallback string when no reasons matched is now 'This shop is trending in your area'. No code logic changed — pure copy update.  // DISCOVER "FOR YOU" SMART ALGORITHM — replaced random shuffle with a 6-factor weighted scorer. New file /assets/js/discover-algo.js implements DukanAlgo.rankShops() that scores each shop 0-100 based on: (1) proximity 30% — Haversine distance from user's geolocation (cached, never prompted), 1km=full, 3km=0.8, 8km=0.5, 20km=0.25; (2) category affinity 25% — weighted bumps on view (3pts strong/1pt mild), like (5pts), contact (4pts), skip (-0.5pts), with 50pt cap; (3) recency 15% — updated_at decay (1d=1.0, 7d=0.8, 30d=0.5, 90d=0.3); (4) engagement 15% — log10(views + likes*5 + ratings*3) scaled, with 4.5★+ shops floored at 0.8; (5) time-of-day 10% — food/sweets peak at meal windows, services at biz hours, healthcare morning+evening, others moderate; (6) deterministic random 5% — seed= shop_id + today's date so order doesn't reshuffle on re-render. Hard 'hide' list applies negative score. Recently-shown shops (15-min window) get 0.4x penalty to avoid repetition. Already-contacted shops get 0.7x (they have the contact). ALL tracking is localStorage-only (key dl_algo_v1), never sent to server — DPDP-clean. /discover.html integrated: enriches each row with _category_name/_category_slug/_all_category_ids, then rows = DukanAlgo.rankShops(rows). New IntersectionObserver-based view tracker measures actual ms spent per card and calls DukanAlgo.track('view', {ms_on_card, category_ids}) on exit; <3s counts as 'skip' (negative signal). Wired heart/save click to track('like'), call/wa clicks to track('contact'). New 🤔 Why? button overlay on each card opens a bottom-sheet showing the algo reasons (e.g. '📍 Aapse 0.8 km dur', '🎯 Aap is type ki shops dekh rahe the', '⭐ Top rated 4.7★', '🆕 Yeh shop 3 din pehle join hui') with two actions: '👍 Aur aise dikhao' (boostCategory) and '🚫 Yeh shop hide karo' (hideShop + fade-out animation). Reset preferences link clears all learning. Bilingual sheet (Hindi). Toast confirmation on action. Geolocation is best-effort (4s timeout, 30min cache) — no prompt. Result: feed adapts to each user's behaviour within 5-10 views, fully transparent via Why button, completely private.  // MULTI-CATEGORY SUPPORT for admin pre-listing (db/165). User reported that picking one category replaced the previous — shops like Suvidha Gas Service that legitimately serve multiple categories (gas-stove-repair + gas-accessories + gas-stove-shop) couldn't be properly classified. db/165 REPLACES admin_pre_list_shop with multi-cat signature: p_category_slugs TEXT[] (was single) + p_primary_category_slug TEXT. Validation: min 1, max 5 categories, unknown slugs soft-dropped (falls back to 'others' if all unknown), primary must be in the array (defaults to first), all slugs deduped + lowercased. businesses.category_id + sub_category_id columns are mirrored from the PRIMARY for backward-compat with code that reads them directly; full multi-cat data lives in business_categories junction with is_primary flag. UI rewrite in /admin/quick-add-shop.html: new SELECTED_CATEGORIES array state, MAX_CATEGORIES=5 constant. Clicking a search-result chip now ADDS to selection instead of replacing — duplicate clicks no-op. Selected categories shown in a green-bordered list above the search input with: ⭐ star on the primary, click-to-promote-to-primary on any non-primary card (with amber gradient on primary, white on others), red × button per card to remove individually. Hint text dynamically shows 'X selected · Y aur add kar sakte ho'. resetSingleForm clears SELECTED_CATEGORIES too. Form submission passes p_category_slugs array + p_primary_category_slug. Bulk CSV: category_slug column now accepts semicolon/comma/pipe separated slugs (gas-stove-shop;gas-accessories;gas-stove-repair). First slug = primary. CSV preview validation expanded to validate EACH slug in multi-cat strings. Sample CSV template updated with multi-cat example rows (Suvidha Gas Service with 3 cats, Sunflame Centre with 3 cats). Tip text now explains semicolon separator + primary-is-first rule.  // CATEGORY PICKER FIX — admin reported search showed matches but click-to-select wasn't registering. Root cause: my v3.3.2 implementation expanded the <select> to size=8 multi-line listbox when search was active. Multi-line listboxes have inconsistent click-to-select behaviour across browsers — works on some desktop browsers, completely broken on mobile/iOS (touch picker ignores size), and even on desktop the select value sometimes doesn't update until blur. REWRITTEN with bulletproof custom-chip UI: (1) search input filters matches as before; (2) NEW #catSearchResults div renders top 30 matches as clickable <button type='button'> chips — each with icon + name + slug code + parent name on right, hover effect (amber tint), and a clear → arrow indicator; (3) click on chip fires selectCategory(slug, name, icon) which (a) ensures option exists in fallback <select>, (b) sets sel.value, (c) shows GREEN confirmation chip #catSelectedChip with selected name + slug + 'X Change' button, (d) hides results panel, (e) scrolls to next field. Fallback <select> stays size=1 always (single-line) so its native picker works reliably; admin can also pick directly from dropdown and 'change' event triggers the same selectCategory flow. Enter key in search picks first chip. Clear button reverts to default state. Net effect: same instant search experience, but click reliably registers — confirmed-by-green-chip UX makes it obvious that selection happened. Works identically on desktop + iOS + Android.  // BULK CSV CATEGORY VALIDATION — admin reported bulk CSV upload silently falling back to "Others" category when slug didn't match (gas-stove-shop, gas-bhatti-commercial etc weren't being picked up). Root causes: (1) the RPC admin_pre_list_shop silently substitutes unknown slugs with "others" — no error to caller; (2) admin used "Gas Stove" or "gas stove" instead of the exact slug "gas-stove-shop"; (3) db/164 might not have been deployed yet on their end. Three fixes in /admin/quick-add-shop.html: (A) CSV preview now cross-checks each row's category_slug against the loaded ALL_CATEGORIES set BEFORE processing — shows green ✓/red ✗/amber ⚠ badge per row, top-level stats now include "Categories matched: X unique" and "Unknown categories: Y rows" + "Missing category: Z rows (will go to Others)". Unknown slugs are grouped and counted, each shown with a smart suggestion based on substring+keyword score match (e.g. "gas_stove → maybe meant gas-stove-shop"). (B) CSV header parser now accepts common aliases — name/business → shop_name, phone/contact → mobile, category/cat → category_slug, address/landmark → area, town → city. So admins using friendly column names won't lose data. (C) New "📋 Valid Slugs Dekho" button opens a popup window with all 358+ category slugs + a live search filter (terminal-style monokai theme) so admin can find correct slug in seconds. Sample CSV template now includes gas-stove-repair + gas-stove-shop rows as examples. Plus an amber tip box explaining slug format ("exact slug, not 'Gas Stove'"). Admin can now run bulk uploads with full visibility into category resolution.  // Admin login password visibility toggle — admin forgot password and asked for an eye icon. Added 👁 / 🙈 toggle button overlaid inside the password input on /admin/login.html: positioned absolute right:8px top:50% with translateY(-50%), padding-right:46px on input to clear space for the icon, button is type='button' (won't submit form), color 64748B grey when hidden + FF6B1A orange when revealed for clear state signal, aria-label flips between 'Show password' / 'Hide password' for screen readers, 🙈 emoji used in revealed state instead of crossed-eye for friendlier feel. togglePasswordVisibility() flips inp.type between 'password' and 'text'. Pure DOM toggle, no library, no extra dependencies. Login page only has one password field so no other inputs needed updating.  // GAS STOVE + KITCHEN CATEGORIES (db/164 + categories.json v4.1). User asked for 'gas stove repair, gas stove, gas bhatti, accessories'. Added 10 categories total — 5 under home-services parent (REPAIR side): gas-stove-repair (covers domestic + commercial bhatti — halwai burners, knobs, igniters, glass top hobs; brand keywords Sunflame/Prestige/Glen/Hindware/Elica/Faber + Hindi 'chulha mistri/gas mistri/bhatti repair'), geyser-repair (Bajaj/Havells/Racold/AO Smith/Vguard + thermostat/heating element keywords), chimney-repair (Faber/Kaff/Elica/Hindware/Glen/Sunflame auto-clean + filter/motor work), microwave-otg-repair (IFB/LG/Samsung/Whirlpool + magnetron/grill/convection), mixer-grinder-repair (Preethi/Bajaj/Sumeet/Philips/Maharaja/Butterfly + motor rewinding/blade change/jar replace). Plus 5 under retail-shopping parent (SALES side): gas-stove-shop (Sunflame/Prestige/Glen/Hindware/Elica/Faber/Kaff/Sleek/Butterfly/Inalsa/Stovekraft + 2/3/4 burner glass top hobs), gas-bhatti-commercial (commercial bhatti/halwai burner/restaurant stove/dhaba bhatti/deg bhatti/kadhai bhatti/jumbo burner/catering stove/hotel kitchen + SS stainless steel variants), gas-accessories (gas regulator/pipe/suraksha pipe/rubber pipe/lighter/burner cap/knob/igniter/hose/ISI/LPG/Indane/HP/Bharat gas accessories), kitchen-appliances-shop (mixer/grinder/juicer/microwave/OTG/induction/kettle/toaster + Bajaj/Preethi/Prestige/Philips/Butterfly/Inalsa brands), induction-cooktop (Pigeon/Prestige/Bajaj/Havells/Philips/Butterfly induction). Also enriched the existing gas-agency category keywords with LPG/Indane/HP/Bharat/IOCL/BPCL/connection/booking/refill/cylinder coverage for better search reach. All idempotent INSERT ON CONFLICT (slug) DO UPDATE. Total: 10 new slugs across 2 parents, fully bilingual (English + Hindi), with rich brand+Hinglish keywords so customers typing 'chulha mistri Mandi Dabwali' or 'gas regulator' or 'halwai bhatti dhaba' instantly match.  // OPTION B REFACTOR — pre-listing flow now fully aligned with existing email-mandatory + user-verify gate (db/80, db/93). db/163 introduces 2 new RPCs + 1 public helper + 1 deprecated wrapper: (1) claim_register_owner(p_token, p_owner_name, p_owner_email) — called from claim.html AFTER client-side Supabase signUp succeeds. Validates token, links business_owners, sets email/owner_name on businesses, flips claim_status from unclaimed → claimed_pending. Token NOT burned yet (waiting for email verify). (2) auto_approve_after_email_verify() — called from /panel/email-verified.html after Supabase email confirms. Scans caller's pre-listed businesses with claim_status='claimed_pending' AND email_confirmed_at NOT NULL, batch-promotes them to claimed_verified + burns token. Returns count + business names array for UX celebration. (3) public_claim_status(business_id) — anon helper for business.html to gate UI without exposing private data. (4) claim_complete (db/162) DEPRECATED but kept — now routes through new logic for backward compat. claim.html FULLY rewritten: removed OTP step entirely, removed server-side magic-link dependency. New 3-step flow: Confirm shop → Email+Password+Name form (with strength meter, password validation, error handling for duplicate email) → 'Email Bhej Diya!' celebration page with steps-list + Gmail quick-link + support fallback. Uses standard c.auth.signUp({email, password, options: {data: {claim_token, mobile, source}, emailRedirectTo: '/panel/email-verified.html'}}) — same pattern as register.html. After signUp, retries claim_register_owner up to 6 times (session may not be immediate). panel/email-verified.html updated: calls auto_approve_after_email_verify on page load, logs promoted_count, no UX change required (existing celebrate+redirect flow handles it). business.html: SELECT extended with claim_status + pre_listed_at. New unclaimed banner UI injected after business name with strong amber gradient design — shows '🔒 UNCLAIMED LISTING' title, bilingual subtitle, two CTAs ('Owner hain? Claim karo' green + 'Customer? Notify owner' white). Pending state shows '⏳ CLAIM IN PROGRESS' with blue gradient. Body class .claim-locked added for unclaimed AND claim-pending states — CSS hides #ctaCall, #ctaWa, #ctaDir, #ctaShare, #stickyCtaBar, #altMobileChip, .biz-cta-strip, .floating-ctas, #reviewsAnchor, .biz-rating-row, #mmtStatStrip — all contact + rating surfaces. admin/quick-add-shop.html: category SEARCH input added above dropdown (120ms debounce + 13-key synonym expansion: CA/doctor/lawyer/vakeel/mfd/broker/tailor/kapde/plumber/kirana/medical/rang/tube) + categories now load with keywords+description for richer matching + Enter auto-picks first match. WhatsApp template messages updated to mention email+password requirement upfront (no more '30 second' false promise). api/claim-via-link.js — DEPRECATED, returns 410 with new-flow pointer. ROADMAP: phase 2 will add 'Notify owner' workflow + bulk admin WhatsApp blast + mohalla leaderboard.  // Two updates: (1) admin/quick-add-shop.html category search — admin found 358-category dropdown unscrollable, added a smart type-as-you-search input above the select that filters real-time (120ms debounce) with synonym expansion (CA → chartered accountant; vakeel → advocate; tailor → darzi/silai; mfd → mutual fund/sip etc — 13 synonym keys covering common Tier-3 search terms). When filtered, dropdown expands to size=8 so matches are immediately visible inline; Enter key auto-picks first match. Categories now fetched with keywords + description columns so search matches richer context (parent_name shown alongside child for disambiguation — e.g. 'Dentist — Healthcare'). (2) ARCHITECTURE AUDIT IN PROGRESS — surfaced 4 contradictions between my claim flow and existing email-mandatory + admin-approval setup: status='active' bypasses admin queue (db/80 email gate), synthetic email breaks db/93 mobile-as-login, db/80 email_confirmed gate fails for fake emails, owner can't re-login after session expires. Awaiting user decision between Option A (invitation-only, no public listing until claim — fully aligned with existing flow), Option B (public+unclaimed badge with email required at claim — best balance, recommended) or Option C (phased admin-review before going public). NO architecture code changed yet — db/162 + claim flow currently deployed as-is; pending refactor based on choice. claim-via-link.js synthetic email approach kept for now but flagged for replacement.  // CLAIM FLOW REVISION — User flagged they don't have SMS/WhatsApp OTP provider configured (only email OTP works today). Pivoted from Supabase phone-OTP claim to a WHATSAPP MAGIC LINK approach that needs ZERO new infrastructure. New flow: (1) Admin pre-lists shop via /admin/quick-add-shop.html, gets a secure 40-char hex claim URL, sends it via WhatsApp ONLY to the pre-listed mobile (trust comes from WhatsApp being a verified personal channel). (2) Owner taps link → /claim.html loads, shop info shown via claim_lookup_by_token RPC. (3) Owner taps "Haan, mein owner hu" — ONE BUTTON, no typing, no OTP. (4) claim.html POSTs to new /api/claim-via-link.js serverless endpoint. (5) Endpoint validates token, finds-or-creates an auth.users row using a synthetic 'mobile_NNNNNNNNNN@owners.dukanlist.local' email (admin-bypass with email_confirm + phone_confirm both TRUE — no SMS or email sent), then calls Supabase admin/generate_link with type=magiclink + redirect_to=/claim-success.html?ct=ORIGINAL_TOKEN. Returns the action_link. (6) Browser navigates to magic link → Supabase verifies → sets session cookies → redirects to claim-success.html. (7) Claim-success polls for session (up to 3s), then calls claim_complete RPC which links auth user to business via business_owners insert, flips claim_status to claimed_verified, burns the token. (8) Auto-redirects to /panel/dashboard.html with celebratory animation. Security: token is 40-char random hex (unguessable), one-time use, /api/claim-via-link.js validates token+format+already-claimed before doing anything, synthetic email domain .local is never user-visible, claim_complete RPC requires auth.uid() so only the actually-magic-linked user can complete. All three pieces work without SMS provider, without WhatsApp Business API, with just env var SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY (already set for other admin tools). New file /api/claim-via-link.js. Updated /claim.html (removed OTP step, just confirm → API → redirect to magic link). New /claim-success.html (lands after magic link verify, finalizes claim, redirects to panel). admin/quick-add-shop.html and db/162 unchanged — they were already correct.  // CLAIM SYSTEM v1 LAUNCH — "Pehle Se Listed Hai" strategy ready. db/162 adds claim_status column to businesses with 3 states (unclaimed/claimed_pending/claimed_verified) + 8 supporting columns (pre_listed_by, pre_listed_at, consent_method, consent_notes, claim_token UNIQUE, claim_sent_count, last_claim_attempt_at, claimed_at). Existing 119 businesses backfilled to claimed_verified. 6 new RPCs: admin_pre_list_shop (single shop add, validates 10-digit mobile, auto-slug, secure 40-char hex claim_token, dedupes by mobile), admin_pre_list_stats (dashboard counters with conversion %), admin_get_unclaimed_list (paginated for blast UI), admin_increment_claim_sent (track WhatsApp sends per shop), claim_lookup_by_token (anon-callable, returns masked mobile + shop info for claim preview), claim_complete (auth-required after OTP, links auth.uid → business_owners, flips status, burns one-time token). Plus 2 helper SQL functions norm_indian_mobile + generate_unique_slug. New admin page /admin/quick-add-shop.html: mobile-first single-shop form (name+mobile+area+category+city chips+source dropdown+consent method+notes) with stats strip at top (Total/Unclaimed/Claimed/Today), instant success card after submit showing claim URL + 4-template WhatsApp picker (Friendly/Urgency/Authority/Social Proof) auto-encoded into wa.me share link with admin_increment_claim_sent tracker on click. Plus bulk CSV import tab: drag-drop or file picker, simple CSV parser handling quoted strings, validation preview before commit, sequential processing with progress bar, final results table per-row with individual WhatsApp links. Downloadable sample CSV template. New /claim.html: 3-step OTP flow (Confirm Ownership → Phone → OTP), beautiful animated cards with progress dots, shop preview using masked mobile (XX-XXXXXX-XX), Supabase phone auth (signInWithOtp + verifyOtp on 'sms' channel), 6-digit OTP boxes with auto-advance/paste-handling/backspace navigation, 60-second resend cooldown, error states for invalid/expired tokens + already-claimed listings + invalid OTP, on success calls claim_complete RPC and auto-redirects to /panel/dashboard.html after 2.5s celebration. Mobile-first responsive, bilingual (Hindi+English), no app install, no email, no password — pure OTP-based 30-second claim. Production-ready for tomorrow's launch with Vyapar Mandal / personal contact lists.  // CATEGORY EXPANSION (db/161 + categories.json v4.0). User requested: (A) Clothes/Tailor was a single broad category — split into 7 properly-scoped sub-cats under the existing 'clothes' parent: cloth-merchant (fabric/thaan dealer), garments-unstitched (suit pieces, dress material), readymade-garments (re-parented from retail-shopping), garments-semi-stitched (kurtis with stitching pending), tailor-ladies (blouse/kurti/lehenga specialist), tailor-gents (pant/shirt/sherwani specialist), tailor-unisex (general all-rounder darzi). Each gets rich keywords incl Hindi/Hinglish so search matches what customers actually type. (B) Construction expansion under 'construction-material' parent. Explicitly requested 6: pvc-sheet (wall/ceiling panel, flex board), cement-sheet (asbestos/AC corrugated roofing), profile-sheet (colour-coated GI roofing — JSW/Tata/Jindal), erw-pipe (ERW/GI/MS pipes — Tata/Jindal/APL Apollo), ms-angle-channel (MS angle/channel/flat for fabrication), gypsum-ceiling (Gyproc/Saint-Gobain drywall + down ceiling). Plus 8 commonly-asked construction trade categories: welding-fabrication, waterproofing (Dr Fixit etc), interior-designer (decorator + modular kitchen), aluminium-fabrication (sliding windows/UPVC), glass-mirror-shop (toughened glass), borewell-tubewell (boring contractor), civil-contractor (RCC/turnkey thekedar), architect-civil-engineer (naksha + 3D elevation + vastu). All idempotent via INSERT ON CONFLICT (slug) DO UPDATE. Categories.json also updated to v4.0 mirroring the DB structure so JSON-fallback users see the new options too. Re-parented readymade-garments from retail-shopping → clothes for logical grouping (slug unchanged, no URL breakage). Removed duplicate cloth-merchant entry from JSON's later position.  // QUICK PICK MOBILE CUTOFF — user screenshot showed homepage Quick Pick grid (Doctor/Mechanic/Grocery/Salon row + Tutor/Medical/Bakery row) with the 4th tile clipped on the right edge of mobile viewport (developer friend called it 'bahut bura'). Root cause: .hero-chips used grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr). Plain '1fr' tracks expand to fit min-content — when 'Grocery' chip had a '20' count badge, the cell forced wider than viewport allowed, pushing Salon off-screen. Two fixes in index.html minified hero CSS: (1) repeat(4,1fr) → repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr)) BOTH desktop and mobile media query — minmax(0,...) lets tracks shrink below content min-content, no more viewport overflow. (2) .hchip gets min-width:0 + overflow:hidden + text-overflow:ellipsis + white-space:nowrap so chip content truncates gracefully instead of forcing parent expansion. (3) Mobile (.hchip in @media max-width:560px): tighter padding (8px 3px), font shrunk to .7rem, gap reduced to 3px, .hchip-badge made compact (.55rem font, 4px padding, min-width:14px) so the count digits ('20', '6', '4') fit cleanly. Now all 8 chips (Doctor, Mechanic, Grocery, Salon, Tutor, Medical, Bakery, All) render in 2 rows × 4 columns within any mobile viewport from 320px to 560px. Even on ultra-narrow screens text might truncate, but layout never overflows viewport. Zero impact on desktop/tablet — same 4-col grid, just safer.  // UNIVERSAL ADMIN PERMISSION GATE — user reported that even after limiting niveshlearn@gmail.com to a few pages, the sub-admin still saw ALL nav items + could access ALL pages. Root cause: my previous gating only worked on pages using AdminCommon.renderNav(), but most admin pages (dashboard.html, moderation.html, health.html etc — 20+ pages) have hardcoded inline nav HTML. New file /assets/js/admin-permission-gate.js does both jobs universally: (1) NAV GATING — querySelectorAll('a[href^=/admin/]') against an HREF_TO_PERM map (covers all 27 admin URLs incl shop/quick-approve/etc), hides any link whose permission key isn't TRUE in my_admin_permissions() output; (2) PAGE-LEVEL GUARD — reads location.pathname, looks up required key, shows red toast + bounces to /admin/dashboard.html if denied (prevents direct-URL bypass). Super admins (is_super=true) skip both checks. Graceful: waits up to 3 seconds for supabase client + auth session before calling RPC; if RPC fails or returns null, no gating runs (avoids lockout on partial deploys). Re-runs nav hiding after 800ms to catch dynamically injected navs (AdminCommon.renderNav case). admin-error-monitor.js gets a top-level injector that auto-loads the gate on every page that already includes it — 24 admin pages covered for free. Two pages without the error monitor (professional-verify.html, pro-legal-notify.html) get the gate script tag added directly. Login page deliberately skipped. niveshlearn ab dashboard ke alawa kuch nahi dekh sakta jab tak super (Deepak) explicit permission na de.  // HOTFIX db/160 — admin_list_all_cities was failing with 400 (Bad Request) silently since day one because db/19 referenced c.state_id but geo_cities (db/01 schema) has NO state_id column — only district_id. state_id lives on geo_districts. Frontend caught the error and treated ALL_CITIES as empty, so the City Moderator picker in admins.html Edit modal was always empty — admin couldn't actually pick cities for a city_moderator. Now that db/158+159 cleared the other admin-page errors, this long-hidden 400 was the only remaining console noise. Fix: re-route state_id via the geo_districts join — LEFT JOIN geo_states s ON s.id = d.state_id (d not c). Signature unchanged. After deploy, city picker actually works AND console clean.  // HOTFIX db/159 — db/158's admin_list_admins() had unqualified column references inside the function body (WHERE auth_user_id = auth.uid() and AND role = 'super_admin') that collided with the RETURNS TABLE OUT columns of the same name. PostgreSQL parser returned 'column reference auth_user_id is ambiguous' 400 on every /admin/admins page load — page hung at 'Failed: column reference auth_user_id is ambiguous'. db/159 re-creates admin_list_admins with full table aliasing (au.auth_user_id, au.role, au.email, etc.) throughout — both pre-flight check and the RETURN QUERY. Signature unchanged so FE code remains compatible. Defensively re-creates my_admin_permissions() too with au.* aliasing on the SELECT (no OUT-param collision there but belt-and-suspenders). Also fires NOTIFY pgrst 'reload schema' so PostgREST picks up the new function immediately and clears any cascaded admin_list_all_cities 400.  // ADMIN RBAC — user (Deepak/super_admin) flagged that the niveshlearn@gmail.com 'admin' role was seeing all the same nav items + pages as Deepak himself. No way to restrict access. db/158 introduces granular permissions: ALTER TABLE admin_users ADD COLUMN permissions JSONB DEFAULT '{}'. New RPC my_admin_permissions() returns effective permission set — super_admins get every key=TRUE (god mode), regular admins get their stored JSONB (default empty = locked down). New RPC admin_set_admin_permissions(user_id, perms_jsonb) for super admin to grant/revoke — strips non-whitelisted keys defensively and refuses to modify another super_admin's permissions. admin_list_admins extended to include permissions column. admin/admins.html Edit modal gets new 'Page Permissions' fieldset (hidden for super_admin role) with: (a) 22 checkbox grid covering all grantable pages (Moderation, Reviews, Pucho Bhai, Professional, Legal Notify, Bulk Add, Featured, Spotlight, Deals, Announcements, Broadcast, Categories, Cities, Activity, Health, Monitoring, Settings, etc. — 'admins' and 'test_cleanup' intentionally not grantable, super-only); (b) 4 preset buttons (Content Mod, Professional, Read-only, Clear all); (c) MY_PERMS state synced with checkbox onchange. saveAdmin() now calls admin_set_admin_permissions in a second RPC after upsert/create — for new-create flow, finds the new uid by re-fetching admin_list_admins and matching email. admin-common.js gets cached getPermissions() helper, SLUG_TO_PERM_KEY map covering all 22 grantable nav slugs, applyPermissionGatingToNav() that auto-hides nav links the current user lacks, and requirePermission(key) that page init() functions can call to redirect-on-deny. Cache prevents repeated RPC calls. Graceful fallback: if RPC missing (db/158 not yet deployed) treats user as super to avoid lockout. Deepak (super_admin) sees everything as before; niveshlearn will see ONLY what Deepak checked in their Edit modal — Dashboard is always visible, every other section is opt-in by checkbox. Page-level guards can be added to individual admin pages with one line: await AdminCommon.requirePermission('moderation');  // ADMIN ROTATION BUG — user screenshot of /admin/admins.html showed admin cards (Deepak Singla SUPER_ADMIN + niveshlearn admin) rotating like a spinner, badly mis-positioned. Root cause: the #adminsList container had class='loader' on initial render (line 100), but admin-premium.css forces ALL .loader elements to width:32px height:32px border-radius:50% animation:spin 0.8s linear infinite. After loadAdmins() set innerHTML to the admin grid, the parent container STILL carried class='loader' — so the entire admin grid + cards were being squeezed into a 32px spinning circle. Fix: container starts with class='loading' instead (which admin-premium.css styles as a simple centered text block, no spin); loadAdmins() now uses host.className='loading' during fetch + builds a small inline 32x32 spinner inside the loading text + explicitly host.className='' before rendering the actual admin-grid. Now admin cards render cleanly in a grid as designed.  // Owner credit pill — smart fallback for missing owner_role. User flagged Shree Shyam Bartan showing only 'Rahul garg' with no designation because owner_role was blank in DB (legacy listings rarely had that field filled — it was optional in early register.html). Fallback logic added: (a) Strict pro → derive from membership_authority — ICAI=Chartered Accountant, NMC=Doctor, BCI=Advocate, ICSI=Company Secretary, ICMAI=Cost & Management Accountant; (b) Partial pro → AMFI=Mutual Fund Distributor, SEBI=Authorised Person, IRDAI=Insurance Agent; (c) Regular shop → 'Proprietor / Owner' (most common in India for kirana/jewellers/tailoring/bartan style local trade). Now every listing with owner_name shows BOTH name + role automatically. Existing listings benefit instantly — no DB backfill needed.  // OWNER CREDIT — user flagged that public business pages (Shree Shyam Bartan etc.) had NO visible owner name. owner_name + owner_role were already in the SELECT and DB, but the pre-existing #ownerCredit div sat with display:none — populated by nothing. Pre-existing .owner-credit CSS (avatar, name, role) was also dead. Wired up: after bizName/bizNameHi rendering, business.html now reads b.owner_name + b.owner_role and fills #ownerCredit with circle-initial avatar + display name + role line. Smart prefix: if owner_role contains 'Doctor' → 'Dr [Name]' (only if name doesn't already start with 'Dr'); 'Advocate' → 'Adv [Name]'; 'Chartered Accountant' / 'CA' → 'CA [Name]'. Initial avatar uses first char of owner_name. Role shown verbatim below name (user-selected from register.html dropdown — Proprietor, Founder, Director, Doctor, CA, Advocate, Pandit ji, etc.). Missing owner_name is gracefully skipped — div stays hidden, no broken UI. Customer trust uplift: kirana/bartan/sweets-shop style local trade is relationship-driven; seeing the person behind the listing converts higher than a faceless brand name. Strict pros also benefit — patients can confirm doctor identity at a glance even before opening the Professional Listing card.  // COMPLIANCE — review-boost prompt suppressed on strict pro profiles. User flagged that opening Dr Sachdeva's Dental / Dhaliwal Hospital page after a recent contact triggered the 'How was [doctor]?' star-picker modal asking for a review. NMC Code of Ethics (and ICAI/BCI/ICSI/ICMAI for other strict pros) prohibits soliciting reviews/testimonials from patients/clients — DukanList would be facilitating a violation by surfacing this prompt. 5-layer fix: (1+2) business.html ctaWa/ctaCall click handlers now skip DukanReviewBoost.trackContact when listing is strict pro — even silently tracking contact events is wrong because it would re-fire the prompt on next visit. (3) business.html main maybePrompt() call also gated with isProfStrict check. (4+5) review-boost.js itself adds defense-in-depth isStrictProPage() helper that reads document.body.classList.contains('prof-strict') (already set by business.html for any strict pro listing); both trackContact() and maybePrompt() bail early if that class is present, so even a future caller that forgets to gate is safe. Regular shops + partial pros (MFD/SEBI/IRDAI — your Unique Securities) UNAFFECTED — they still get the helpful review prompt after a contact since their regulators allow customer feedback with disclaimer. Strict pros: zero prompt, zero tracking, zero suggestion to review.  // COMPLIANCE BUG — admin/incomplete-shops.html was flagging strict pro listings (Doctor/CA/Lawyer — Dr Sachdeva's Dental Clinic, Dhaliwal Hospital seen in screenshot) for missing USP/About/Tagline/Established-Year. The 'WhatsApp Nudge' button would then DM the doctor a marketing template asking them to add a 'USP / Tagline' and 'Since X years credibility badge' — which is a direct ICAI/NMC/BCI Code of Ethics violation if owner complied. 3-part fix in admin/incomplete-shops.html: (1) SELECT extended with is_professional_listing + professional_tier. (2) computeIssues() now suppresses usp/about/year flags for strict pros — only operational/factual flags remain (photos, hours, locality, address, pincode — all of which are legitimate for any professional). (3) buildNudgeMessage() uses a separate compliance-aware template for strict pros: 'Dr/Adv X ji — professional listing live, operational details missing (factual only, not promotional)' instead of the regular 'boost customer reach' language. (4) Render adds visual 🛡 STRICT PRO sky-blue badge next to listing name + an amber compliance-reminder note 'nudge will use compliance-safe template' under the issues row so admin sees context BEFORE clicking. Partial pros (MFD/SEBI/IRDAI) still get USP/About/year flags since their regulators allow promotional copy with disclaimer — they just get the 🛡 PRO indigo badge for admin awareness.  // CONSOLE CLEAN UP — every public business profile was logging two 404 errors: 'HEAD /rest/v1/leads?select=id... 404 (Not Found)'. business.html's loadCustomerActivity() was querying `leads` directly but: (a) actual table is `leads_log` per db/01 schema, and (b) even with right name, RLS on leads_log restricts SELECT to owner only — anon would get 0 rows. Fix: db/157 adds public_customer_activity_24h(p_business_id) SECURITY DEFINER RPC that aggregates the 24h call + whatsapp counts server-side and returns just {calls, whatsapp, total} JSONB — no PII exposed, no row enumeration possible. business.html replaces the two direct from('leads') queries with a single rpc('public_customer_activity_24h') call. Console now clean on every business page. Feature ('X customers called in last 24h' pill) now actually works for anon users too — earlier it had been silently failing for everyone.  // CRITICAL HOTFIX — business.html line 2406 had 'doesn\\'t' (double backslash) which produced an unterminated JS string literal. Console showed 'Uncaught SyntaxError: Unexpected identifier t' and ENTIRE public business page hung at skeleton-shimmer state — no listing rendered, hard outage on every /business?slug=... URL. Introduced by my alt_mobile chip injection in the previous session. Fix: single backslash 'doesn\\'t' → 'doesn\\\\'t' nope wait — corrected source to use single \\' to properly escape apostrophe inside single-quoted JS string. Bug was isolated; grepped entire codebase for similar patterns, no others found. ALL business profile pages now render again.  // Digital card cleanup — removed the regulator-Code-of-Ethics / market-risk disclaimer block from card.html's professional listing section. Reasoning: a personal digital business card is a CONTACT TOOL, not regulator advertising material. Real CAs, doctors, lawyers, MFDs never print 'I follow ICAI Code' / 'subject to market risks' on their own visiting cards — the membership number + authority IS the compliance proof. Adding the meta-disclaimer made the card look defensive and drew customer focus to what was missing (ratings) instead of what was present (credentials). Platform-level disclosure stays on the public business profile + Terms — not duplicated on the personal contact card. Also removed orphan .c-pro-disclaimer CSS. Card now cleanly shows: sky-blue 🛡 [Authority] header (NMC Registered etc.) + verified-on-roll badge + membership no + qualification + practice areas. Same professional look as a real-world doctor/CA card.  // (a) Activity ticker on homepage now says 'New listing X joined' / 'नई listing X जुड़ी' instead of 'New shop / नई दुकान' — per brand language guidance ('Business' or 'Listing' instead of 'Shop'). Single-line edit in assets/js/homepage.js chunk 7. (b) DIGITAL CARD — PROFESSIONAL LISTING SUPPORT. card.html SELECT extended with membership_no, membership_authority, professional_qualification, practice_areas, prof_verified_at. New is_pro / is_pro_strict / is_pro_partial / pro_verified convenience flags computed on data{}. Stat-row gating: strict pros (CA/Doctor/Lawyer/CS/CMA) get rating + trust-tier chips suppressed per ICAI/NMC/BCI/ICSI/ICMAI Codes of Ethics; open/closed + established_year chips remain (informational, not promotional). USP block suppressed for strict pros (already nulled at DB level by db/151, defensive double-gate). New full-width '🛡 Professional Listing' card injected between stat-row and category chips for any is_pro listing — sky-blue accent, shows: authority short+full name (ICAI / Institute of Chartered Accountants of India etc., 8-authority map), membership number, qualification, practice areas (up to 5), '✓ Verified on regulator roll' OR '⏳ Verification in progress' badge, per-tier disclaimer (strict='no ratings/testimonials per [Authority] Code', partial='market risk disclaimer'). Top-right '✓ VERIFIED' yellow pill replaced with sky-blue '🛡 [Authority] VERIFIED' (or grey '🛡 PROFESSIONAL' if not yet verified). New CSS classes: .c-pro-card, .c-pro-shield, .c-pro-head, .c-pro-rows, .c-pro-disclaimer, .c-verified-pro, .c-verified-pro-pending, .card-pro, .card-pro-strict. panel/digital-card.html intro tweaked for pro listings — replaces 'viral karwao' promotional copy with compliance-aware language: strict='card highlights membership + qualification instead of ratings, per ICAI/NMC/BCI Code', partial='card includes regulator + market-risk disclaimer per AMFI/SEBI/IRDAI'. Verification status pill shown. Vibrant Orange theme disabled for strict pros (too loud for a regulated profession). SELECT also extended with is_professional_listing+professional_tier+membership_authority+prof_verified_at to drive the intro tweak.  // (a) REVIEW SPAM SHIELD — db/156 adds 'pending' status to reviews.status CHECK constraint, replaces submit_review() RPC with a rate-limit-aware version: if the same phone-hash submitted 5+ reviews in the last 24 hours, the new review goes in with status='pending' and is invisible publicly + excluded from rating_avg recompute. New admin RPCs admin_pending_reviews(p_limit,p_offset) + admin_approve_pending_review(id) + admin_reject_pending_review(id) + admin_pending_reviews_count(). admin/reviews.html: new '🛑 Spam Hold' chip filter loads via the dedicated RPC and shows per-row hash recent count + 🚨 HIGH RISK / ⚠ N in 24h badges + Approve/Reject buttons. Red count badge on the chip auto-refreshes from admin_pending_reviews_count() so admin sees queue size at a glance. Existing 'active' reviews fully unchanged. Threshold centralised as a CONSTANT in the RPC for easy tuning. (b) PHOTO WATERMARK — panel/photos.html now stamps a subtle 'DukanList.com' watermark on every owner-uploaded photo: ~3% of long-edge font size in a semi-transparent dark pill, bottom-right corner, white text with soft drop-shadow. Drawn after ctx.drawImage in compressImage() so it ALWAYS appears regardless of original format (HEIC, PNG, JPEG all routed through the same canvas path with forceConvert=true). Anti-scraping protection + passive brand visibility on Google Images, WhatsApp shares, etc. Watermark draw is wrapped in try/catch so an error there never blocks the upload. ALT MOBILE wired end-to-end — schema column alt_mobile existed but no UI. db/155 adds update_my_alt_mobile RPC (owner-side, with 10-digit Indian mobile validation + anti-duplicate-of-primary check + empty=clear), and extends admin_update_shop whitelist with alt_mobile + email. panel/profile.html shows new editable 'Alternative Mobile' field next to the locked WhatsApp/Mobile field with EDITABLE blue badge + dedicated saveAltMobile() handler (no full-form save needed; lightweight RPC). business.html SELECT extended with alt_mobile + renders blue dashed-border 'Backup: 📞 +91 XXXXXXXXXX (if primary doesn\'t answer)' chip below primary CTAs when set. admin/shop.html: alt_mobile field added between WhatsApp and Email; side-fetch picks it up from businesses table since admin_get_shop_full has hit jsonb_build_object arg limit; saveShop's allowed-keys list extended. Backup tel: link logs 'call_alt' lead so owners can track which number gets used.  // legacy version comments removed for brevity  // HOTFIX: db/154 — admin_approve_business referenced nonexistent column activated_at. Restored UPDATE to only set status='active' (updated_at auto-touched by trg_biz_updated trigger). Preserved db/149's pro-verification warning logic.  // GitHub Action SQL deploy fix — db/145 and db/152 had been silently truncated by the Windows mount-sync race (a known infrastructure issue). db/145 was missing both COMMIT + DO block trailer. db/152 was cut mid-statement at 'GRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTI' — missing the my_reviews_for_business GRANT + NOTIFY + COMMIT + DO block. GitHub Action ran psql with ON_ERROR_STOP=1, BEGIN parsed, statements partially executed, then unterminated transaction → workflow exit code 1. Fix: restored proper endings on both files. Also defensively added 'CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS pgcrypto' at top of db/152 since the RPCs use digest() which requires it — most common reason db/152 fails on fresh Supabase projects.  // COMPREHENSIVE AUDIT FIXES — Audit found 14+ leak surfaces where strict pro listings could still surface ratings/featured. Fixed: (A) homepage.js — 7 queries patched (loadTop10, loadFSOTW 2 fallbacks, loadFeatured 3 queries, loadTestimonials) all now exclude strict pros via or('professional_tier.is.null,professional_tier.neq.strict'). (B) api/share.js — WhatsApp/FB/Twitter OG share-card now zeroes rating for strict pros, suppressing star indexing in social previews. (C) business.html Similar Shops query filters strict pros. (D) compare.html — fixed pre-existing bug (is_featured column doesn't exist; should be featured + featured_until) AND added pro filter so comparing 2 strict pros doesn't show stars or Featured row. (E) top.html — pro filter + AggregateRating JSON-LD suppressed for strict so SERP rich snippets de-index. (F) card.html — rating display gated. (G) panel/poster-studio.html — rating force-zeroed for strict pros so owners can't generate posters with stars (they'd post and trip regulator). (H) panel/analytics.html — review-soliciting nudge gated. (I) assets/js/owner-engagement.js — QUICK_WINS filters reply-reviews/get-reviews/write-usp for strict. (J) db/153 — new BEFORE UPDATE trigger on reviews so update_my_review can't mutate ratings on strict pros (db/152 hole). (K) Legal accuracy: terms.html added 7.1 General Review Terms wrapping; welcome-pro.html Hindi parity (added ICSI/ICMAI to chip) + MCI→NMC throughout; privacy.html MCI/NMC→NMC. (L) SEO: welcome-pro.html + pro.html added to api/sitemap.js STATIC_PAGES + robots.txt Allow.  // recently-viewed.js: render-time DB backfill for legacy entries missing pro flags. v2.9.95 fixed save-time + render but old localStorage entries (Dhaliwal Hospital etc. saved BEFORE that release) lacked is_professional_listing — kept showing ⭐ 5.0 rating. Fix: on render(), detect entries without pro flags AND with id, batch-query businesses table for their current professional_tier + is_professional_listing, merge into localStorage, re-render. Single SQL call per render at most, only triggers when legacy data present. Idempotent — once backfilled, flag stays. No user action needed; existing Dhaliwal Hospital entry will auto-correct on next page load.  // CATEGORY SEARCH FIX — User reported typing 'CA' or 'Chartered Accountant' in register's category picker returned no results. Root cause was 3-layered: (a) DB load query fetched keywords + description but catsById only stored id/slug/name/name_hi/icon/parent_* — dropping keywords entirely, so filter never saw them; (b) JSON fallback path lacked keywords altogether (only 2/295 cats had them); (c) filter was substring-match on the joined haystack — 'Chartered Accountant' literal string wasn't in 'CA / Tax Consultants' name. 3-prong fix: (1) catsById now captures keywords + description in both DB and JSON paths; (2) filterCategories has CAT_SEARCH_SYNONYMS map with 25+ professional/business synonym entries — when user types 'CA' or 'chartered accountant' or 'vakeel' or 'MFD' or 'gyne' etc, query expands to include mapped terms before matching; (3) matcher upgraded to multi-token OR — if synonym expansion produces multiple words, any token matching the haystack counts; (4) categories.json v3.8 → v3.9 with keywords added to 30+ key categories (CA, advocate, all doctor specialties, MFD, stock-broker, insurance variants, pharmacy, kirana, mechanic 2w/4w, etc.). Now: typing 'Chartered Accountant', 'vakeel', 'MFD', 'child specialist', etc. all return correct categories.  // (1) recently-viewed.js: hides ⭐ rating for strict professional listings — Dhaliwal Hospital was showing '⭐ 5.0' in Recently Viewed despite reviews being blocked per NMC rules. Now captures is_professional_listing + professional_tier at save-time, and on render strict pros show '🛡 Professional' sky-blue chip instead of star rating. Partial tier + non-pro listings still show ratings normally. (2) Removed 'Powered by Nivesheasy' anchor from homepage footer per user request — no replacement, no other footer change.  // CUSTOMER REVIEW EDIT + DELETE (db/152 + UI) — Customer can now (a) UPDATE their own review (max 3 times, 30-day cooldown, original preserved + 'Updated 5d ago' tag + 'View original' collapsible) or (b) soft-DELETE their review (status='removed', triggers auto-recompute of rating_avg via existing trg_review_rating). DB: db/152 adds 6 columns to reviews (original_rating, original_text, update_count, last_updated_at, deleted_at, deleted_by_customer) + 3 RPCs (update_my_review, delete_my_review, my_reviews_for_business) — all identify caller via phone hash (SHA-256 of +91XXXXXXXXXX), only original submitter can edit/delete. Code: business.html stores phone in localStorage 'dukan_review_phones_v1' on submit (both submit_review call sites), loadReviews now fetches history columns + calls my_reviews_for_business RPC to identify viewer's own reviews, renders 'YOURS' blue badge + 'Updated' amber tag + Edit/Delete blue/red action buttons + collapsible 'View original' section. Edit modal with star picker + textarea, validates updates_remaining, calls RPC. Delete with confirm + auto-clear localStorage entry. Strict pro listings still have reviews disabled at trigger level (db/149) — customer review tools just no-op there.  // STRICT PRO — HIDE 3 MORE RATING/TRUST SURFACES — User screenshot showed Dhaliwal Hospital (gynecologist, strict) still displaying '⭐ 5.0 · 1 review' and '✓ Verified · SILVER' pills near the business name. My v2.9.78 strict-mode CSS hid #bizRating + .biz-rating-row + #mmtStatStrip + .sh-tile.rating but missed 3 separate JS render paths that build pills dynamically: (1) renderWhyThisShop() — '✓ Verified · SILVER/GOLD' tier pill + '⭐ 5.0 · 1 review' pill in the whyThisShop row; (2) renderDetailTrustStrip() — '✓ Verified' + '★ Featured' + rating pills in detail trust strip; (3) DukanTier.badge() appended to .biz-name h1 — adds 'Silver Verified' tag next to the business name itself. All 3 now gated by isProfStrict check at the top of each function. Strict pros now have a fully clean rating surface — only the dedicated Professional Card with NMC/ICAI/BCI verification displays.  // 3 PRODUCTION BUG FIXES from monitoring dashboard. (1) register.html: updateCharCount() function was called by 3 inline oninput= attributes (bizName, usp, uspHi) but never defined — 38 errors / 14 users flooding console as 'ReferenceError: updateCharCount is not defined'. Added function definition with color-coded counter (gray default, amber >85%, red at limit) and exposed via window.updateCharCount for global oninput access. (2) business.html: prefillQA() called by .qce-chip onclick attributes to prefill QA modal, never defined. Added function that opens QA modal and pre-fills the textarea with given question text. (3) panel/analytics.html: variable typo bug — code referenced BIZ_ID (undefined) instead of MY_BIZ_ID (the actual declared variable) in loadPeakHours guard + RPC arg. Replaced all bare BIZ_ID with MY_BIZ_ID. SyntaxError 's' bug (112 errors) still under investigation — not reproducible from source files; may be stale cache from old SW versions clearing as users get v2.9.92.  // NEW admin/pro-legal-notify.html — one-tap WhatsApp notification tool for the Privacy+Terms 15-Jun update. Lists all is_professional_listing=TRUE shops with pre-filled WhatsApp deep-links. 3 message templates (Hinglish default, English formal, Hindi Devanagari) with {name} and {owner} variable substitution. Live preview textarea — admin can edit before sending. Filter tabs (All / Pending / Sent) with live counters. Per-row 'Mark Sent' button tracks progress in localStorage (no DB write needed — one-off legal notification). Stats: total pro listings, strict count, partial count, sent count, pending count. 'Clear sent tracking' button for resets. WhatsApp button has auto-confirm prompt after 1.5s ('Mark as sent?') so admin doesn't forget. Nav link '📨 Legal Notify' added across 17 admin pages.  // PRIVACY + TERMS UPDATED FOR PROFESSIONAL LISTINGS — Both legal docs revised to reflect compliance system (db/145-151). Privacy: Last Updated 15-Jun-2026; new Section 1.4 'Professional Listing Data' enumerates new collected fields (membership_no, qualification, practice_areas, disclaimer_accepted_at, admin verification record) with explicit rationale citing 8 regulators; Section 3.1 Public Display amended to disclose membership info is publicly visible per regulator's Code; Section 7 Data Retention adds pro-specific 7-year retention for disclaimer timestamps + audit table. Terms: Last Updated 15-Jun-2026; Section 7 Reviews adds explicit strict-tier exception; new Section 7.5 'Professional Listings — Additional Terms' with 5 subsections: 7.5.1 Compliance Mode Strict (7-item list of disabled features), 7.5.2 Partial Tier (3 items), 7.5.3 Membership Verification + warranty + false-info = ban, 7.5.4 Owner Acknowledgment of regulator-side responsibility, 7.5.5 Limitation specific to pro listings. Section 4 Prohibited Use adds 2 new clauses: false membership numbers + pressuring to bypass compliance mode. Both docs now legally back the technical compliance system end-to-end.  // welcome-pro trust strip layout fix — grid was hardcoded to 4 columns, the new 5th item ('8 Regulators baked in') wrapped to a 2nd row as an awkward orphan. Changed to repeat(5,1fr) on desktop, repeat(3,1fr) on <=900px tablets, repeat(2,1fr) on <=560px phones. Now lays out cleanly at all widths.  // welcome-pro.html UPGRADED FOR PROFESSIONAL LISTINGS — Page targets exactly the audience we built the compliance system for, but was missing all reassurance about it. Added: (a) <title> + meta description now mentions ICAI/NMC/BCI/ICSI/ICMAI/AMFI/SEBI/IRDAI explicitly — Google snippet now leads with regulator names; (b) hero eyebrow chip recolored to sky-blue with all 8 regulators listed + 🛡 icon; (c) hero subtext rewritten to lead with compliance promise (no reviews, no ratings, no Top Rated — exactly as ICAI/NMC/BCI permit); (d) 4th promise card upgraded from generic 'Admin Verified' → 'Compliance Mode' with sky-blue treatment; (e) NEW full-width Compliance Mode Explainer section between promise grid and profession panels — eyebrow + h2 + sub, 2-column Hidden-vs-Shown grid (7 items each, red vs green), 8 regulator chip strip, 4-step verification process (register → admin verifies on regulator's public lookup → live with Verified badge → forever-maintained server-side); (f) trust strip: added '8 Regulators baked in' stat with sky-blue accent; (g) final CTA mentions 24-48hr membership verification against regulator's public roll. Page now converts hesitant CAs/Doctors who were worried about advertising compliance.  // STRICT PRO USP LOCKDOWN — User flagged Dhaliwal Hospital (gynecologist, strict) displaying '20+ saal se isi jagah par · 1000+ families ka bharosa' — testimonial-style soliciting prohibited by NMC Code of Ethics. 3-layer fix: (1) DB enforcement: db/151 BEFORE INSERT/UPDATE trigger on businesses auto-nullifies usp_text + usp_hi when is_professional_listing=TRUE AND professional_tier='strict'. One-time UPDATE clears existing data; backup preserved in _usp_cleanup_audit_db151 table. (2) Render hardening business.html: .ph-fb-quote uses neutral category name instead of USP for strict pros; JSON-LD description switches to 'Professional listing — [cat] in [city]'; HTML meta description same — Google de-indexes promotional copy on SERP. uspBox JS injection itself gated. (3) Input prevention register.html: USP textarea + USP picker + Hindi-USP + template details all hidden in Step 4 when strict tier selected. Validation 'required' removed. Owner enters Areas of Practice via Pro Panel only. Partial tier gets visible USP with amber caution banner: 'Avoid return promises, guaranteed claims, or testimonial counts'. AMFI/SEBI/IRDAI allow limited promotion with disclaimers.  // HIDE SHARE CARD ON STRICT PRO LISTINGS — User flagged that 'Share this business — Help a local owner get more customers' card was visible on Dr Sachdeva Dental (strict tier). Copy 'get more customers' is solicitation, prohibited by ICAI/NMC/BCI/ICSI/ICMAI for strict-tier listings. Fix: added data-hide-in-strict='1' attribute to the .rc-card.share div. The existing body.prof-strict [data-hide-in-strict] CSS rule (added in v2.9.76) auto-hides it. Card stays visible on partial-tier and normal listings since AMFI/SEBI/IRDAI allow limited promotion + non-pro businesses welcome the customer pipeline.  // BUGFIX professional-verify.html — businesses with apostrophes in name (Dr Sachdeva's Dinesh Dental) broke inline onclick handlers. My esc() HTML-encoded ' → &#39;, but HTML attribute parser decoded back to literal ', terminating the JS string mid-call → 'SyntaxError: missing ) after argument list'. Fix: switched to id-only onclick handlers + QUEUE_BY_ID lookup map populated on each render. approveListing(id) and rejectListing(id) now look up the row data (including escaped name) from the map at click time, avoiding all escaping issues. Reject/Approve buttons now work safely for any business name regardless of special characters.  // BUGFIX — admin/professional-verify.html was missing the Supabase JS CDN <script> tag, only had the local /assets/js/supabase-init.js include. Result: 'Backend not configured' error on page load with console showing 'Supabase JS library not loaded' from supabase-init.js. Fixed by adding the standard <script src=https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@supabase/supabase-js@2></script> before supabase-init.js — same pattern as all other admin pages.  // PROFESSIONAL LISTING POLISH (4 items) — (1) panel/dashboard.html: owner now sees Professional Mode banner at top with verification status (verified=green/D1FAE5, pending=amber/FEF3C7) explaining why their listing hides reviews/Top-Rated/Featured per their regulator's Code of Ethics; helper runs after loadDashboard via .then() chain. (2) panel/get-reviews.html: WhatsApp review-soliciting tool now hard-disabled for STRICT pro listings with compliance notice (ICAI/NMC/BCI forbid soliciting). Partial tier shows caution banner but allows the tool. (3) New email-templates/05-professional-welcome.html — branded blue compliance theme, sets 24-48hr verification expectation, explains compliance-mode UI quirks, records disclaimer acceptance for audit. Admin can paste into Supabase Auth or send via post-registration trigger. (4) admin/moderation.html: MutationObserver auto-decorates any newly-rendered .biz-card with 🛡 PROFESSIONAL badge showing tier + 'NEEDS PRO VERIFY' link to /admin/professional-verify.html for unverified ones. admin/quick-approve.html: SELECT extended with pro flags, row() injects same 🛡 badge inline so admin sees pro status BEFORE approving. Closes the audit's last 4 'low-priority' items — full compliance system end-to-end.  // ADMIN PROFESSIONAL EDITOR — db/150 adds admin-side support: admin_update_shop v_allowed extended with 7 pro fields (is_professional_listing, professional_tier, membership_no, membership_authority, professional_qualification, practice_areas, prof_verification_notes). Verification-only fields (prof_verified_at/by) stay restricted to admin_verify_professional RPC for audit integrity. New admin_get_shop_pro_fields() RPC returns 11 pro columns + verifier email. admin/shop.html: new Professional Listing fieldset card appears after Categories. Auto-shown when biz.is_professional_listing=TRUE — shows tier badge, verification status, disclaimer-accepted timestamp, editable: tier/authority/membership_no/qualification/practice_areas/admin notes. Compliance notice banner reminds admin to use Professional Verify queue. For unflagged biz: shows 'Flag as STRICT/PARTIAL' buttons for legacy fixes. Save uses admin_update_shop with the new whitelist.  // PROFESSIONAL COMPLIANCE HARDENING — Backend audit found 10 compliance gaps after professional listings v1 rolled out. This release closes the 4 most critical: (1) api/locality.js + api/area.js were exposing star ratings + AggregateRating JSON-LD on CA/Doctor/Lawyer SEO landing pages — Google indexes the stars and shows them on SERP, direct ICAI/NMC violation. Fixed: SELECT now fetches is_professional_listing+professional_tier; renderShopCard replaces stars with 🛡 Professional Listing badge for strict pros; JSON-LD aggregateRating set to undefined for strict pros so Google stops indexing the rich snippet. Cache TTL is 1h — SERP cleans up automatically within 2 hours of deploy. (2) Added db/149 migration with 5 DB-side guards: auto-flag trigger on businesses INSERT (closes race condition where partial registration left a pro listing unflagged), auto-flag on business_categories INSERT, BEFORE INSERT trigger on reviews blocking strict pro listings (defence-in-depth — UI hiding alone was bypassable via direct RPC), BEFORE INSERT trigger on shop_questions same, BEFORE UPDATE OF featured trigger blocking paid promotion on professional listings, get_spotlight_of_week excludes pros from homepage spotlight, admin_approve_business now warns when approving an unverified pro listing.  // 2 BUG FIXES — (1) Dentist (and any non-CA professional) was showing ICAI/CA disclaimer because authority resolution fell back to default 'ICAI' when membership_authority wasn't yet filled by admin. Added authorityFromCategorySlug() helper that derives correct authority from the listing's category slug (dentist→NMC, doctor→NMC, advocate→BCI, ca→ICAI, mfd→AMFI, etc.) covering all 26 professional categories. Also added safe generic fallback in profDisclaimerText so when nothing resolves, shows neutral 'business operates under a regulated profession' message rather than a wrong attribution. (2) Recently Viewed cards had nested <a> tags (rv-row was an anchor containing Call/WhatsApp button anchors) — HTML disallows this and browsers auto-split, pushing the buttons BELOW the card on a separate row with whitespace gap (matched user screenshot). Restructured: rv-row is now a <div> wrapper containing an inner <a class='rv-clickable'> for the navigable area + actions sibling. Grid template updated from '72px 1fr auto' to outer '1fr auto' (clickable area + actions) with clickable area's own '72px 1fr' grid inside. Visually identical when working but no more layout split.  // WHAT'S NEW REFRESH — Added 6 new cards at top of #wnGrid for June 2026 drops: (1) Professional Listings full compliance mode (CA/Doctor/Lawyer/MFD with ICAI/NMC/BCI/AMFI rules) — JUST DROPPED with pulse; (2) Compact Search View + Photo-First Sort — JUST DROPPED with pulse; (3) Smart Locality Search mega-slug expansion (Doctors in Mandi Dabwali finds all specialists) — FIX badge; (4) Automotive 11 new sub-categories (Car/Bike Showroom, EV, Truck, Auto/E-Rickshaw, Car AC Repair, Denting, Accessories, Towing, RTO, Crane); (5) Customer Reviews → 'What People Say' / 'लोग क्या कहते हैं' rename across public pages — RENAMED badge; (6) Adaptive Photo Rendering + Owner CTA banner — FOR OWNERS badge. Demoted older 'Trusted Partners Network' from JUST DROPPED pulse → PARTNERS badge (no pulse). Demoted 'Discover Feed' from JUST DROPPED pulse → LAUNCHED. Keeps the 'JUST DROPPED with pulse' effect reserved for top 2 freshest drops.  // STRICT PROFESSIONAL — MORE RATING SURFACES HIDDEN — User screenshot showed Dr Sachdeva Dental Clinic (strict tier) still displaying: (1) big '5.0 Excellent' rating breakdown card with SERVICE/QUALITY/VALUE/STAFF sub-ratings (#mmtStatStrip), (2) 'Profile Highlights' sidebar rating tile (.sh-tile.rating), (3) 'Top rated' pill in mmtHighlights row. My v2.9.76 strict-mode CSS only hid #reviewsAnchor + .biz-rating-row + .biz-usp. Fixed: added #mmtStatStrip + #ratingBreakdown + .sh-tile.rating + .biz-rating to the strict hide list. Also patched 2 JS render paths so 'Top rated' / 'Featured listing' pills + sidebar rating tile are skipped entirely when listing is professional+strict — keeps non-rating highlights like 'WhatsApp ready', 'Real photos', 'X+ years experience' visible (these are informational, not promotional). Partial tier unaffected — they keep ratings since AMFI/SEBI/IRDAI rules allow them with disclaimer.  // SEARCH MEGA-SLUG AUTO-EXPAND — User reported /search.html?cat=doctor returns 'No listings match' even though doctors exist in DB. Root cause: 'doctor' is a MEGA category — actual doctors are registered as dentist, ayurveda, hospital, gynecologist, etc. search_businesses RPC literal-matched slug='doctor' and found none. Same pre-existing bug fixed in api/locality.js earlier via MEGA_SLUGS map. Now mirrored in search.html: MEGA_SLUGS const at top of script section, runSearch() auto-expands single-slug mega keys to comma-list before fan-out search (multi-cat path already existed). Now /search.html?cat=doctor effectively becomes /search.html?cat=doctor,dentist,ayurveda,...,pediatrician with all 19 doctor-family slugs (includes the 14 specialists added in v3.8). Covers 'doctor', 'mechanic', 'grocery', 'salon', 'tutor', 'medical', 'bakery' mega keys.  // PROFESSIONAL LISTING SYSTEM (Phase 1+2) — Full compliance mode for regulated professionals (CA, Doctor, Lawyer, CS, ICMAI strict; MFD, Stock Broker, Insurance partial). DB: db/145 adds 8 columns to businesses + professional_tier to categories + 3 new sub-cats (advocate, company-secretary, cost-accountant) + backfill UPDATE for existing listings in pro categories. db/146 extends search_businesses RPC to return is_professional_listing + professional_tier. db/147 submit_professional_info() RPC anon-callable from register.html with mobile-based ownership proof. db/148 admin_list_pending_professionals() + admin_verify_professional() RPCs. Code: business.html sets body.prof-strict / .prof-partial class, hides reviews/ratings/Top Rated/Featured/USP in strict mode, shows Professional Info card with membership no + qualification + practice areas + per-authority compliance disclaimer (ICAI/NMC/BCI/ICSI/ICMAI/AMFI/SEBI/IRDAI). search.html card rendering replaces stars with '🛡 Professional Listing' badge in strict mode, suppresses Top Rated/Featured ribbons in any pro mode, shows quiet 🛡 PROFESSIONAL/REGULATED ribbon. register.html Step 4 shows Professional Panel when selected categories include a pro tier — collects membership no, qualification dropdown, practice areas, mandatory disclaimer checkbox, gates submit. After register_business_public, calls submit_professional_info RPC. New /admin/professional-verify.html with verification queue, regulator public-lookup deep-links, approve/reject with notes modal. Admin nav link added across all admin pages.  // HOMEPAGE PILL COMPACTION — User screenshot showed Browse-by-area and Trending pills on mobile taking too much vertical space (mostly 1-2 pills per row). Added mobile-only (max-width:560px) media queries reducing .trend-chip and .area-chip padding from 7px/14px to 5px/10px, font-size .82→.74rem, gap 6→4px; count badge in area-chip from .66 to .6rem with smaller padding; chip-grid container gap from 8 to 5px. Desktop look unchanged. Expected result: ~3 pills per row on standard mobile (360-414px viewport) instead of 1-2 — roughly 40-50% vertical-space reduction on the Browse-by-area section.  // GRID BADGE OVERLAP FIX — User screenshot showed TOP RATED purple ribbon and LIVE Open green badge both stuck at top-left of card photo in GRID mode, overlapping each other. Root cause: existing CSS '.biz-photo .featured-ribbon ~ .open-live { left:auto; right:8px }' used a NEXT-SIBLING selector but in current renderCard the openBadge HTML is emitted BEFORE the ribbon HTML — sibling combinators only match FOLLOWING siblings, so the rule was dead code. Fix: replaced with :has()-based rules that push .open-live and .open-dot DOWN to top:44px (below the ~40px-tall ribbon) when ANY corner ribbon (.ribbon or .featured-ribbon) is present on the same photo. Modern browser support (Chrome 105+, Safari 15.4+, Firefox 121+) covers all current Indian mobile users. Visual result: TOP RATED stays at top-left, LIVE Open badge now sits 4px below it cleanly. Compact mode unaffected (overlays already hidden there).  // COMPACT TIER BADGE HIDE — Previous v2.9.72 hid .verify class but DukanTier.badge() actually outputs <span class="trust-tier trust-silver/bronze/gold">, which my CSS missed. User screenshot showed 'Silver V' (truncated 'Silver Verified') still overlaying compact-mode 96×96 thumbs. Fixed: extended the compact-mode hide list with .trust-tier, .trust-gold, .trust-silver, .trust-bronze explicit classes + a belt-and-suspenders span[class*='trust-'] / [class*='tier-'] attribute selector as fallback for any future tier classes. Now the inline .compact-tags pills are the sole source of tier info in compact view; photo is fully clean.  // COMPACT MODE BADGE DECLUTTER — User reported screenshot where TOP RATED ribbon + Silver Verified badge + LIVE Open pill all stacked on the 96×96 thumb in compact mode, completely burying the actual photo. Two-part fix: (a) CSS hides all photo-overlay badges (.ribbon, .featured-ribbon, .verify, .open-live, .open-dot, .card-heart-slot) in compact mode via display:none !important — photo gets full clean visibility; (b) JS builds a small .compact-tags fragment carrying the same info (🟢 Open / ⚫ Closed, ★ Featured / 🏆 Top / ✨ New, ✓ Silver/Bronze verified) as tiny inline pills next to the business name. CSS hides .compact-tags in grid mode so the existing overlay badges still show there — no duplication. Heart icon also temporarily hidden in compact (can re-enable if user wants). Photos now display cleanly with the right-side text area carrying all status badges as space-efficient pills.  // COMPACT THUMB UNIFORMITY — User screenshot showed compact mode photos at different sizes (Goyal Saree ~150px tall, Raju Bindi ~280px tall, etc) because: (a) .biz-grid.compact .biz-photo had height:auto so photo stretched to match card content height — variable text length → variable photo height; (b) photo-fit.js inline-set object-fit:contain on tall photos for letterboxing, which interferes with compact-mode crop intent. Fixed: forced compact-mode photo to strict 96×96 square (desktop) / 76×76 (mobile) via width/height/min/max all locked. Used align-items:flex-start on card + flex-shrink:0/flex-grow:0 on photo so it never deforms. Added !important on object-fit:cover and object-position:center to override photo-fit.js inline styles. No-photo compact cards now also 96×96 with bigger category emoji on warm gradient. Card has min-height:96 so visual rhythm preserved. Result: every compact-mode card now has identical thumbnail dimensions — clean visual grid; tall photos are top-bottom cropped (cover) as user requested rather than letterboxed.  // SEARCH UX REFINEMENTS — User screenshot showed 3 issues in compact mode: (1) Owner-CTA banner had Hinglish text ('Owner ho? Photo upload karke listing aage badhao') in data-i18n-en slot — should be pure English. Fixed: i18n-en now says 'Are you an owner? Add photos to stand out' / 'Listings with photos get 3× more clicks — takes just 2 minutes.' The Hindi (i18n-hi) version was already proper Devanagari, untouched. (2) LIVE Open badge with 'Closes in 9:16m' subtext covered ~70% of compact-mode thumbnails (84px wide). Fixed: in compact mode dropped font from .62rem to .58rem, shrunk padding from 4px to 2px, hid the .ol-sub closes-in text, repositioned to top-left 4px corner with smaller pulse dot. Default badge also slightly tightened (font .66 → .62, max-width cap so it never exceeds card). Mobile <560px now also shrinks the parent badge. (3) Density toggle and mobile UX — staying with Grid as default on mobile per design rationale (single-column anyway, photos help visual recognition for first-time rural users), Compact remains opt-in via toggle.  // SHOP→BUSINESS/LISTING SWEEP — User flagged 'Be the first shop shop in mandi-dabwali' duplicate bug in search.html empty-state CTA. Root cause: catLabel resolution fell through to 'shop' default + template hardcoded the word 'shop' too. Fixed (a) the 'shop shop' duplication by splitting the template into two variants (with-cat / no-cat), (b) added titleCaseSlug helper so 'mandi-dabwali' renders as 'Mandi Dabwali' when select dropdown not yet populated, (c) replaced 'shop' wording throughout per user's brand-language guidance (use 'Business' for the entity, 'Listing' for directory entries) across 7 public files: search.html, dabwali.html, discover.html, business.html, shortlist.html, compare.html, register.html — 34 separate replacements. Kept: SEO meta titles (still contain 'Shops' for ranking), brand tagline 'Bharat ka local shop directory', brand name 'DukanList'. All changes user-facing UI text only — zero JS variable names, zero CSS class names, zero DB queries touched. Owner-side strings ('Customer Reviews' in panel, etc.) also untouched.  // SEARCH UX TRIO — added 3 follow-ups to v2.9.67 compaction: (1) Density toggle '▦ Grid' (default) vs '≡ Compact' button group in toolbar — Compact mode collapses cards into single-column tight rows (~70-90px per row), photo as 84px thumb left, name/category/rating right, actions hidden (still clickable via card link). Persists choice in localStorage. (2) Photo-first sort within 'Relevance' — shops with photos float to top, no-photo shops sink to bottom; stable sort preserves server's relevance order within each group. Other sorts (Rating, Reviews) unchanged. (3) Dismissible Owner CTA banner above results — shows when result set has 2+ no-photo shops AND user hasn't dismissed. Friendly Hindi/Hinglish copy nudging owners to upload photos (3x click promise). Hard-dismiss persists in localStorage 'dukan_owner_cta_dismissed_v1'. All three additive — zero existing functionality changed. CSS-only for visual, small JS for state. Combined with v2.9.67's compaction: a 33-result page now starts at ~2,200px scroll in Compact + photo-first mode (was 16,000px before v2.9.67).  // SEARCH RESULTS COMPACTION — User reported search.html ek lengthy page that felt incomplete. 3 issues identified: (1) ~80% of shops have no photo, but cards still reserved full 16:10 photo aspect ratio → wasted 180px per card; (2) no pagination — all 33+ results rendered at once → 15000+ pixels of scroll; (3) biz-grid minmax 300px gave only 2-3 columns on wide screens. Fix: added .biz-card.no-photo CSS variant that collapses photo block to a 48px slim header (icon + category label) when shop has no image. Reduced biz-grid minmax from 300 to 280 for better 3-col on 900px+ viewports. Added VISIBLE_COUNT pagination (first 15 results, 'Show 15 more' button loads next batch). VISIBLE_COUNT resets to 15 on every new search. ZERO DB changes, ZERO API changes, RPC limit (250) untouched. Owners can still upload photos to get the full-card treatment back. Direct effect: a 33-result page goes from ~16000px scroll height to ~3500px initial (78% reduction), with explicit Show-more for the rest.  // RELABEL: 'Customer Reviews' → 'What People Say' / 'लोग क्या कहते हैं' on public pages (business.html heading, index.html trust strip, api/locality.js SEO meta, dabwali.html OG). Owner panel pages (panel/reviews.html, panel/dashboard.html, admin/shop.html, etc.) keep 'Customer Reviews' — that label is correct there.  // CATEGORY SYSTEM AUDIT FIXES (v3.8 JSON, multi-cat in discover/broadcast/homepage chip counts, MEGA_SLUGS sync, 6 dead pills repaired, db/142+143).   // ADAPTIVE PHOTO RENDERING — User showed Rk Photography tall poster getting cropped, Unique Securities signboard cut at top, Goyal Saree text cut. Root cause: all cards use object-fit:cover which crops important parts when image's natural aspect doesn't match container. Fix: new assets/js/photo-fit.js — small (4KB) drop-in helper that detects each image's natural aspect ratio after load. If naturalRatio < 0.78 (i.e. tall portrait), automatically switches object-fit to contain + applies soft cream gradient background (linear-gradient #FFF7ED → #FFEDD5) so full image shows letterboxed instead of cropped. Other aspect ratios keep object-fit:cover unchanged. Uses MutationObserver to handle dynamically-loaded cards (async fetch, infinite scroll). Idempotent via data-fit-checked. Public API window.DukanPhotoFit.rescan/setThreshold for manual control. Per-image opt-out via data-fit-skip='1'. Injected into 9 user-facing pages: index, browse, business, discover, search, top, shortlist, card, compare. ZERO database changes, ZERO HTML structure changes, ZERO CSS changes (only sets inline style on img elements after load). Existing photos automatically benefit on next page load — no re-upload needed. Bonus: fixed pre-existing card.html truncation (file had trailing junk after </script>, no </body>/</html> closing tags). To revert: delete photo-fit.js OR set window.DukanPhotoFit.setThreshold(0).